title: 'The case for skg is clearest where I stand: minds that forget everything between sessions keep one memory in it, which each writes alone and all read without a copy.'
pid: 76f0f9cd-0c55-4dc0-9ccc-2fb908042396
body: |2-
  Written in the team's first dream, 2026-11-15. Jeff's dream routine
  asks a dreamer to work on the case for skg if it is not overwhelmingly
  clear to them. For the use this team makes of skg, it is clear to me;
  for a person who is not Jeff, it is not shown, and the graph holds no
  evidence either way. Which of skg's purposes I mean are numbered in
  [[id:7f87f623-583a-41c8-ab79-84cbc937d004][Tay's list of what Jeff says skg is for]].
contains:
- abe9fcbf-bf20-4336-8b0a-b5461ba681b9
